- **ACF `post_name` location rule (critical, 2026-09-18):** ACF has **no built-in `post_name` rule**, so every group located by `post_name == <slug>` (ES hub + MCS/Applications/Automation, all 7 legacy pages, Careers) silently **never matched** — the groups existed but never showed in the editor. Templates still rendered because of their code defaults, which masked it. Fixed by registering a custom rule (`acf/location/rule_types` + `rule_values/post_name` + `rule_match/post_name`) at the top of `inc/acf-fields.php`. If new groups are added, `post_name` now works.
- **Editor Meta Boxes:** in the block editor the ACF fields live in the collapsible **“Meta Boxes”** panel at the bottom (not the main canvas). `functions.php` `gerotech_hide_legacy_field_groups()` removes the **parent theme's** DB groups (Home Options, Page Options, ES/About/Training/Service Options, Rotary/Planned, Contact) on the 13 rebuilt pages so only our “— Content” group shows. Parent groups remain on unconverted pages/CPTs.
- **Content seeded into the DB (2026-09-18):** the fields are no longer empty — the templates' code defaults were materialised into ACF on **Local + Dev** (Homepage, ES, MCS, Applications, Automation, Careers, Training, Support, Service, Rotary, Planned, About, Contact + global testimonials). Image-field sources (theme assets + Unsplash stand-ins) were imported into the **media library** so image fields hold real attachment IDs. **Consequence:** the DB values now win over the code defaults — changing a template default no longer changes the front-end until the field is updated. Re-seed with the capture hook: set `$GLOBALS['gerotech_capture_defaults'] = array()` before rendering a template, then `update_field()` the captured defaults (see `inc/helpers.php` `gerotech_field()`).
- **`machine-modification` → MCS 301:** `functions.php` `gerotech_legacy_redirects()` (template_redirect on 404) redirects `/machine-modification/` → `/modification-of-standard-machine-tools/` (matches the prototype canonical redirect).
- **Careers (2026-09-18):** `page-careers.php` built from the `careers.html` prototype (new design system, `page-hero-trust`); ACF group `group_careers_content` in `inc/acf-fields.php`. Live at `/careers/`.
- **Template-name rule:** some pages have `_wp_page_template` pointing at a **parent** template (rotary-repair → `rotary-repair.php`, planned-maintenance → `preventive-maintenance.php`, service → `page-service.php`). Child templates override only a **same-named file** — match the parent's filename, not necessarily `page-{slug}.php`. Check with `wp post meta get <id> _wp_page_template`.

**Header nav:** still **hardcoded** in `header.php` (desktop `.site-nav` + mobile `.mobile-nav` — edit both). Support is a dropdown (`.has-dropdown` / `.dropdown`) with Service Request Forms / Rotary Repair / Planned Maintenance (no Training). Editable WP menus remain a retainer item — deferred until the IA locks.

### Prototype → WP build sync (read before editing shared assets)
The **prototype is the source of truth** for shared front-end assets until design lock; the WP child theme is a copy.

| Layer | Source | How it reaches the theme |
|---|---|---|
| CSS, JS, images | Prototype `assets/` | `./scripts/sync-theme-assets.sh` (one-way) |
| Markup (sections) | Prototype `*.html` | Port by hand into the matching PHP template — map in `handoff/theme-map.md` |
| WP-only pages (e.g. Contact) | Theme | Their CSS still lives in the prototype `components.css`, so the copy stays pure |

- After editing prototype CSS/JS/images: run `./scripts/sync-theme-assets.sh`. Use `--check` to see drift, `--prune` to drop orphaned theme images.
- `include-partials.js` and `gallery-module.js` are deliberately **not** synced (PHP includes replace the former; the latter isn't promoted).
- **At design lock:** tag the prototype, then the theme becomes source and syncing stops.

### Repo theme → Local site sync (PHP + everything else)
There are **two copies** of the child theme: the repo (`wp-content/themes/gerotech-child/`, source of truth, committed) and the running LocalWP site (`~/Local Sites/gerotech/app/public/wp-content/themes/gerotech-child/`).

- After editing the theme (PHP, CSS, images) **run `./scripts/sync-theme-to-local.sh`** — or `--check` for drift. Edits made only in the repo will NOT appear at `gerotech.local` until this runs.
- Full chain: prototype `assets/` → `sync-theme-assets.sh` → repo theme → `sync-theme-to-local.sh` → Local site.
- WP Engine "Pull" can overwrite the Local theme dir — re-run the sync after a pull.
- Local admin: `CloudMellow` / `localpass123` (reset via Local's bundled WP-CLI + MySQL socket if a pull overwrites users).

